# Line endings are normalised to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Terraform deploys the Glue job scripts with source_hash = filemd5(...),
# which hashes the bytes on disk. Without this file, a Windows checkout gets
# CRLF and a Linux CI runner gets LF, so the same commit produces two
# different hashes and every CI plan reports phantom changes to the script
# objects in S3. eol=lf makes the checkout byte-identical everywhere.
#
# text=auto still lets Git detect binary files and leave them alone.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.py text eol=lf
